      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "The force required to loosen a bolt varies inversely with the length of the handle of the wrench used. This means that the product of the force and the length of the handle is a constant. We can set up the equation as follows:\n\nForce × Length = Constant\n\nLet's call the constant \"C\". Then we have:\n\nForce₁ × Length₁ = Force₂ × Length₂\n\nWe know that the force required to loosen the bolt is 375 pounds when the handle length is 9 inches. So, we can substitute these values into the equation:\n\n375 × 9 = Force₂ × 15\n\nNow, we can solve for Force₂:\n\nForce₂ = (375 × 9) / 15\n\nForce₂ = 3375 / 15\n\nForce₂ = 225\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require 225 pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
