      "sample_index": 5,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the concept of inverse variation. In an inverse variation, the product of two quantities is constant. Here, the force \\( F \\) and the length of the handle \\( L \\) are inversely proportional, so we can write:\n\n\\[ F \\times L = k \\]\n\nwhere \\( k \\) is a constant.\n\nFirst, we need to find the value of \\( k \\) using the given values. We know that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force. So, we can write:\n\n\\[ 375 \\times 9 = k \\]\n\n\\[ k = 3375 \\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\( k \\), we can use it to find the force required for a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches. Let \\( F' \\) be the force required for a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches. Then:\n\n\\[ F' \\times 15 = 3375 \\]\n\nTo find \\( F' \\), we can solve for it by dividing both sides of the equation by 15:\n\n\\[ F' = \\frac{3375}{15} \\]\n\n\\[ F' = 225 \\]\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require \\(\\boxed{225}\\) pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
